  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/5e4e2241490626139e15800f3b90c8e15a9963bdcace9907f8557b0897d533e6.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $p(0)$ is positive.\n- $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n- $x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=0,$ which means that $p(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
